libstdc++ 13's <format>: the four inline std::vformat overloads
(format:3784/3793/3802/3811) were dropped with "scope '__format' is
ambiguous" -- see test.desc (header-free, CORE).  The later drops are
fixed too: format:1422 and format:3124 _M_visit
(cpp11_lambda_closure_per_template_specialization), _M_parse_format_spec
(cpp11_specialization_distinguishes_fundamental_types) and format:1899
(cpp11_member_template_argument_converted_to_non_deduced_parameter); bin53
dropped more than ten bodies.  g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.
broken-libstdcxx16: with libstdc++ 16 (16-20260315), _M_reserve and _M_span
of <format>'s _Seq_sink lose their bodies (KNOWNBUG
cpp20_hidden_friend_spaceship_template_alias_return_type); the earlier drop
of __do_vformat_to no longer occurs (checked 2026-10-26).
